  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CEGORN-Prevention bad effects of alcohol</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main goal of the project is to raise legal awareness to reduce alcohol abuse in the community and violations of the law on preventing harmful effects of alcohol, thereby contributing to improving the quality of life with the reduction of social crimes and social gap in the locality. The project sites cover 4 communes in Quang Binh, namely Thuong Hoa, Trong Hoa, Dan Hoa (Minh Hoa district)and Lam Hoa (Tuyen Hoa district). The target groups include under-18 children, women, girls and people of ethnic minorities. Project activities focuses on:1. Implementing communication campaigns in multiple platforms for students (12-17) and the community to raise public&apos;s awareness about the harmful effects of alcohol and related legal regulations2. Organizing awareness raising trainings forpeople, especially men, about the harmful effects of alcohol and illegal acts3. Providing legal aid and representation at court forsurvivors of domestic violence and sexual abuseOverall, the output is expected to have 2000 - 3000 people including women, boys andgirls, people of ethnic minorities, people living in (near) poverty, teachers at schools in the project area with increasing legal awareness on prevention of harmful effects of alcohol and alcohol use; 80% of people and students with better access to legal consulting services; 100 business households receiving legal advice directly related to the legal provisions on prevention of harmful effects of alcohol.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Centre for Highland Natural Resourc</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Established in 2015, Centre for Highland Natural Resource Governance Research (CEGORN) is a Science and Technology organization under the Vietnam Union of Science and Technology Associations (VUSTA). CEGORN has its operation focus on matters related to policy andlaw, involving activities to raise people&#x2019;s awareness. It embraces great respect and appreciation towards indigenous knowledge, presented by its efforts and investment in analysis and integration of indigenous culture into actions to promote sustainable development. In addition to great hands-on experience in working with people of ethnic minorities, CEGORN staff are all well equipped with thorough understanding about women&apos;s rights, thereby, encourage them to raise their voices and contribute to promote gender equality. In terms of project management, CEGORN has its capacity to harness resources, which contributes to enhance the effectiveness of the project implementation.
